{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545494-v20-developing-thaumaturgy-in-a-vacuum","id":1545494,"title":"V20: Developing Thaumaturgy in a Vacuum?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-06T15:00:06-08:00","id":1545494,"title":"V20: Developing Thaumaturgy in a Vacuum?","content":"The topic says it all: Given enough time and resources, could a vampire with no knowledge of Thaumaturgy develop it? Assume a Mage type background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T15:10:44-08:00","id":1545495,"title":"","content":"Yes, the same way if given enough time a person could reinvent binary coding or invent the abacus. Individual vampires did invent Thaumaturgy in the first place. The real question is did a ghost teach early necromancers or spirits teach the first koldunic sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-09T19:06:38-08:00","id":1545635,"title":"","content":"Yep. I would say that without the influence of teachers who already know blood magic one would have a more limited portfolio of Paths and Rituals available to develop than, say, a Tremere apprentice or an Assamite neonate of the Sorcerer caste, but pretty much all the forms of vampiric blood magic are based on the principles of wider occult traditions in the human world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-09T22:14:45-08:00","id":1545636,"title":"","content":"Yes, in the same way someone without a background in science could become a physicist, virologist, or geologist. Amateurs can become skilled at disciplines just like professionals, it just takes a lot more time and dedication since they don't do so through a credentialed path with others mentoring them. They still need access to occult resources, texts, and other publicly available knowledge which are probably hoarded by people already in the know, but it is possible to do so. It's not impossible, but I wouldn't make it easy on any PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T11:56:17-08:00","id":1545657,"title":"","content":"There's isn't much I can add to the topic, but yes it's possible for a Kindred to learn Blood Sorcery on their own through trail and error and even possibly coming up with new rituals or variations on older spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T03:53:54-08:00","id":1545682,"title":"","content":"I agree with the previous answers.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, it's down to creativity and occult knowledge to examine existing occult traditions and figure out how one can have a point of access. I take those to be Intelligence and Occult.<br /> <br /> Depending on what they try to do specifically, they would have access to different forms of Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: the following is based on the game lore, not on real world Hermetic magic or magic of other kinds. For example, real world astral magic isn't represented very well in the game lore, and so-called Hermetic magic is a hodgepodge of different things, including, but not limited to,astral magic.<br /> <br /> Tremere Thaumaturgy works through Will, Blood and Sympathy. That's not too hard to come up with if one peruses plenty of manuals of Hermetic magic: one has to figure out that Vitae, on top of sustaining you, can also magically empower your Will, which is otherwise dead like your body, unlike human sorcery (unless the ST rules that sorcery, as opposed to awakened magic, is available to vampires anyway). The real difficulty here is believing with conviction that this can indeed work, long enough to put in the required effort to see consistent, reassuring results instead of giving up and becoming convinced that it's impossible. If one was a Mage before the Embrace, it's easier. If one knows some details about Tremere Thaumaturgy, it's easier, because it gives one more confidence to keep trying.<br /> <br /> Assamite Sorcery, or Dur-An-Ki, is based on ancient covenants between the first Sorcerers of Banu Haqim and spirits. One would need to come across an Incantation (available to vampires as well, at least in VDA20) suitable to evoke a particular spirit capable enough to grant the would-be sorcerers the powers of Paths and Rituals related to his purviews, or at least enable him to communicate with other spirits higher up the chain. That's not terribly hard, and I can think of ways this would be accessible to Muslim vampires too, because of some practices where, by calling a certain Name of Allah in specific ways over a period of time, different creatures, including the celestial bodies, are happy to speak, befriend and assist the person as long as they stay pious. They may, however, dislike vampires, and it may also be that the modality of said invocation of the Divine Names does not fit a vampire's sleep schedule. At the end of the day, the deal presupposes a social interaction with spirits and an agreement of sorts (I assume the original agreement of the Assamite Sorcerers was the sacrifice of blood, hence why the expense of 1 blood point).<br /> <br /> Egyptian Setite Sorcery (Akhu) is based on perverting ancient Egyptian funerary rites and having some deal with whoever is or is posing for Set, or somehow forcing the other Egyptian gods to help. Setite sorcery also has other forms, depending on the cultural background of the given Setite. So one may be creative.<br /> <br /> Indian Thaumaturgy as well as Wanga are very much tied to they cultural context, but in principle Indian Thaumaturgy is an issue of Will and invoking Names of deities, and Wanga is a bit similar to Dur-An-Ki or Akhu in its being connected to spirits. Same for Koldunism. Necromancy is something else, but I'd say it's taught by the dead or by spirits of death.<br /> <br /> Other forms are conceivable. Ultimately it's down to what tickles player and ST's fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}